# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository *and* check it out as LF on
# every platform.
#
# The `eol=lf` half is the part that matters here. With `core.autocrlf=true` and
# no .gitattributes, a Windows working tree gets CRLF on checkout while the repo
# stays LF — which makes `prettier --check` fail on files that are perfectly
# fine, because Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`. Pinning the working tree
# to LF keeps the formatter, the repo, and CI agreeing on all three platforms.
#
# This is a no-op for repository content: everything tracked here is already LF
# in the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never normalize, never diff as text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data, not source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw game logs come from the laser tag system as-is. Currently gitignored, so
# this only guards against an accidental commit — but if one ever lands, its
# bytes must survive untouched.
*.tdf -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drizzle hashes each migration's SQL to decide whether it has already run, so
# these bytes must stay stable — a line-ending flip would change the hash and
# re-trigger applied migrations. Stated explicitly so it survives any future
# change to the global rule above.
packages/db/drizzle/*.sql text eol=lf

# Collapsed in GitHub diffs and excluded from language stats. Still diffable.
packages/db/drizzle/meta/** linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml              linguist-generated=true
